<title>USA: Scantek has 10 pct of HumaScan.</title>
<headline>Scantek has 10 pct of HumaScan.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scantek Medical Inc said Friday that it now owns 779,000 shares, or 10 percent, of its U.S. licensee HumaScan Inc, following HumaScan's recent public offering.</p>
<p>HumaScan completed an initial public offering of 2.7 million shares at $6 per share on August 14. HumaScan is also the Canadian licensee for Scantek.</p>
<p>Before HumaScan's public offering, Scantek owned 20 percent of HumaScan, said Scantek spokesman Joe Mansi.</p>
<p>Scantek has a patented breast cancer detection device called &quot;BreastAssure,&quot; which Scantek said has received U.S. Food and Drug Administration authorization for marketing.</p>
</text>
